Configuring a hadoop cluster is a complex business, there are tens of parameters, maybe more. Those are whirr parameters, so you haven't even started with that line. Some Hadoop defaults are a little puzzling to me to.

> Also is it correct, after firing up the hadoop proxy...to ssh into the jobtracker node to run my R code or is there a way to do that from the machine that launched the cluster? as this would be preferable for my needs.

Again this is not rmr specific, since hadoop can adopt a remote client  configuration like the one you want, it surely can be done. I work on EC2 and I got tired of figuring out firewall issues instead of doing my work, so I just ssh in.

>
> Also it was interesting that by increasing the size of the vector your got it to use more nodes to carry out the map function, is there a way to get it to always use the 4 nodes no matter that the size of the vector? i.e. to always equally distribute the tasks....

My understanding is that even if there is a parameter calle mapred.map.tasks that you can set very high, Hadoop is not bound to respect it and will only consider it among other factors in setting the actual number of map tasks. Again, a question for a Hadoop forum.

Antonio

