The repo is for developers, not general users. The download page is here https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki/Downloads

The downloads can be installed as they are. The install procedure knows which directories to use for what. Don't let me discourage you for developing an interest in the structure of R packages though. The reference document is http://cran.r-project.org/doc/manuals/ <http://project.org/doc/manuals/>R-exts.html

The main page of the wiki is the place to start. https://github.com/RevolutionAnalytics/RHadoop/wiki

>
> As for Revo, Can you clarify what are the required/recommended options for the Revo R installation?

 Unfortunately I am not the right person and this is not the best channel to get answers on that. I would suggest contacting Revo's support.  For Academic license I gather from their web site: "This offer only covers the Revolution R Enterprise software itself. Academic Users may receive free support from the Revolution Discussion Forums <http://forums.revolutionanalytics.com/forum.php> and inside-R.org <http://www.inside-r.org/> Community Web site. Premium Technical Support <http://www.revolutionanalytics.com/support/> options are available for an extra fee."

> In particular, is RevoScaleR a required option or simply an automatic part of Revo R?

RevoScaleR is not required to use RHadoop, other than that I am not sure.

